{# Training Effect (Training Metrics, since 2026-10-25; was a tile scoring
   the Your Swim workout, then briefly in Highlights): how much your latest
   logged swim did for your fitness, 0.0 to 5.0. Its load comes from
   intensity (pace against your threshold pace, stroke-adjusted), duration
   and stroke, then it's compared with your typical logged swim of the
   last 6 weeks. Members only. Filled by swim-tools-v2.js (renderTraining).
   Display only. #}
<article class="swim-card swim-effort" id="training-effect">
  <div class="swim-summary__heading">
    <h3 class="swim-summary__title">Training Effect</h3>
    <p class="swim-summary__lead" data-st="teSwim"></p>
  </div>
  <span class="swim-kpi__value"><span data-st="teValue"></span><span class="swim-kpi__unit"><span data-st="teWord"></span></span><span class="swim-effort__felt" data-effort-felt hidden>You rated it <b data-st="effortFelt"></b>/10</span></span>
  {# Peak effort (4.5 and up): a caution about overdoing it #}
  <p class="swim-te__warn" data-te-warn hidden><i class="fa-solid fa-triangle-exclamation" aria-hidden="true"></i><span data-st="teWarn"></span></p>
  <p class="swim-summary__fine swim-effort__sub" data-st="teSub"></p>
  {# Locked, until 5 swims are logged in the last 6 weeks: a faded sample
     reading behind how many more to log (swim-tools-v2.js) #}
  <div class="swim-te-lock" data-te-lock hidden>
    <span class="swim-te-lock__teaser" aria-hidden="true">2.5 <span class="swim-kpi__unit">Steady</span></span>
    <p class="swim-te-lock__title" data-st="teLockTitle"></p>
    <p class="swim-te-lock__text" data-st="teLockText"></p>
    <div class="swim-te-lock__dots" data-te-lock-dots aria-hidden="true"></div>
    <button type="button" class="btn btn-primary btn-sm" data-modal-target="#swimDeckLog">Add to Log</button>
  </div>
</article>
